    "protected": false,
    "rendered": "<div class=\"xyz-content\">\n<nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"shell pt-6\">\n<ol class=\"m-0 flex list-none flex-wrap items-center gap-2 p-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">\n<li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\">  <a href=\"/\" class=\"no-underline hover:underline\"> Home </a> </li>\n<li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"> <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-rule\"> / </span> <a href=\"/calculators/\" class=\"no-underline hover:underline\"> Calculators </a> </li>\n<li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"> <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-rule\"> / </span> <span aria-current=\"page\">HECS-HELP</span> </li>\n</ol>\n</nav>\n<div class=\"shell pt-6\">\n<p class=\"band-eyebrow\">Free calculator</p>\n<h1 class=\"max-w-3xl text-3xl sm:text-4xl\">HECS-HELP repayment calculator</h1>\n<p class=\"mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[1.0625rem]\">Repayments went marginal on 1 July 2025. Enter your income and see what actually comes out — and roughly how long the debt takes to clear.</p>\n<p class=\"m-0 font-mono text-[0.75rem] tabular-nums text-ink-soft mt-4\"> Updated for 2024–25, 2025–26, 2026–27 · verified against <a href=\"https://www.ato.gov.au/tax-rates-and-codes/tax-rates-australian-residents\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ato.gov.au</a> on 2026-08-21 · some 2026–27 thresholds are provisional pending ATO indexation </p>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"shell mt-8\">\n<div id=\"xyz-island-0\" data-xyz-island=\"HelpCalculator\" data-xyz-props=\"{&quot;defaultFy&quot;:&quot;2026-27&quot;}\">\n<div class=\"grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_23rem] lg:gap-12\">\n<div class=\"min-w-0\">\n<div class=\"rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-4 sm:px-6\">\n<div class=\"py-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] last:border-b-0\">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3\"><label for=\"_r1R_2l_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Your repayment income</label></div>\n<div class=\"mt-2\">\n<div class=\"relative\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 font-mono text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">$</span><input id=\"_r1R_2l_\" type=\"text\" inputMode=\"decimal\" autoComplete=\"off\" class=\"w-full rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-ink)] focus:border-[var(--color-signal)] pl-7 text-right\" placeholder=\"0\" value=\"85,000\"/></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Start with your salary. Add salary-sacrificed super and any reportable fringe benefits.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"py-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] last:border-b-0\">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3\"><label for=\"_r1R_4l_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Your loan balance</label></div>\n<div class=\"mt-2\">\n<div class=\"relative\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 font-mono text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">$</span><input id=\"_r1R_4l_\" type=\"text\" inputMode=\"decimal\" autoComplete=\"off\" class=\"w-full rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-ink)] focus:border-[var(--color-signal)] pl-7 text-right\" placeholder=\"0\" value=\"28,000\"/></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Optional — used only to estimate how long the debt takes to clear.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"py-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] last:border-b-0\">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3\"><label for=\"_r1R_6l_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Financial year</label></div>\n<div class=\"mt-2\"><select id=\"_r1R_6l_\" class=\"w-full rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-ink)] focus:border-[var(--color-signal)]\"><option value=\"2024-25\">2024–25</option><option value=\"2025-26\">2025–26</option><option value=\"2026-27\" selected=\"\">2026–27</option></select></div>\n<p class=\"mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">2024-25 used the old flat rates; 2025-26 onwards is the marginal system.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"mt-4\">\n<div class=\"rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white p-5\">\n<h2 class=\"m-0 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]\">2026–27<!-- --> repayment scale</h2>\n<table class=\"mt-3 text-[0.8125rem]\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Repayment income</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Repayment</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$0<!-- --> – $69,528</th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\">Nil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$69,529<!-- --> – $129,717</th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\">15% of the excess</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$129,718<!-- --> – $186,050</th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\">$9,028 + 17% of the excess</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$186,051<!-- -->+</th>\n<td class=\"font-mono\">10% of total income</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"min-w-0 lg:sticky lg:top-6 lg:self-start\">\n<div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white\">\n<div class=\"flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-[var(--color-ink)] px-4 py-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-paper)]\">Study loan</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.6875rem] tabular-nums text-[var(--color-paper)]/70\">2026–27</span></div>\n<div class=\"tally-print\">\n<div data-tally-line=\"income\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] \">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Repayment income</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums \" aria-hidden=\"true\">$85,000</span></span></div>\n</div>\n<div data-tally-line=\"threshold\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] \">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Less the threshold</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">−</span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums \" aria-hidden=\"true\">$69,528</span></span></div>\n</div>\n<div data-tally-line=\"assessable\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)]\">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Income that counts</span><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums font-semibold\" aria-hidden=\"true\">$15,472</span></span></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div data-tally-line=\"repayment\" class=\"px-4 py-5\">\n<div class=\"flex items-end justify-between gap-4\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"m-0 text-[0.8125rem] font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Compulsory repayment for the year</p>\n<p class=\"m-0 mt-0.5 max-w-[22rem] text-[0.6875rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">That is 2.73% of your repayment income, at a marginal rate of 15%.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"flex h-11 shrink-0 items-center\"><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-[var(--color-owing)]\" aria-hidden=\"true\">$2,321</span></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"sr-only\" aria-live=\"polite\">Compulsory repayment for the year<!-- -->:<!-- --> <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$2,321</span></p>\n<p class=\"m-0 mt-2 font-mono text-[0.6875rem] tabular-nums text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">15% on the income above your band</p>\n<div class=\"mt-4\">\n<div class=\"space-y-3\">\n<p class=\"m-0 rounded-[3px] bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)] px-3 py-2 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">At this income the debt clears in roughly<!-- --> <strong class=\"font-mono tabular-nums text-[var(--color-ink)]\">13</strong> <!-- -->years, before indexation and before any pay rises.</p>\n<p class=\"m-0 text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">An estimate, not tax advice. Indexation is applied by the ATO on 1 June each year and is not modelled here.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div data-testid=\"sticky-result\" class=\"fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-40 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white/95 backdrop-blur lg:hidden\">\n<div class=\"mx-auto flex max-w-[68rem] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3\">\n<div class=\"min-w-0\">\n<p class=\"m-0 truncate text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Yearly repayment</p>\n<p class=\"m-0 font-mono text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-[var(--color-owing)]\">$2,321</p>\n</div>\n<p><a href=\"https://brsadvisory.myassembly.com/login?step=signUp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"shrink-0 rounded-[4px] bg-[var(--color-ink)] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-paper)] no-underline\">Lodge</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"h-20 lg:hidden\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n<p><!--astro:end--></div>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"shell mt-8\">\n<p class=\"m-0 max-w-2xl text-[0.8125rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft\"> This is an estimate, not tax advice. It works from the figures you enter and the ATO rates for the year you selected; your actual assessment is determined by the ATO and may differ. We never ask for your tax file number on this site. </p>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"shell mt-16\">\n<div class=\"prose-statement\">\n<h2>What changed on 1 July 2025</h2>\n<p> The old system applied a single percentage to your <em>whole</em> repayment income. Earning one dollar over a threshold moved you to a higher rate on every dollar you earned, so a <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1</span> pay rise could cost several hundred dollars. It was the clearest example of a genuine tax cliff in the Australian system. </p>\n<p> The marginal system removed it. Nothing below <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$69,528</span> counts. Above that, 15c in each dollar up to the middle band, then 17c above it. Because only the excess counts, a pay rise can never leave you worse off. </p>\n<h2>Why your repayment is higher than you expected</h2>\n<p> Repayment income is not your salary. The ATO adds back reportable fringe benefits, any super you salary sacrificed, exempt foreign employment income and net investment losses. A negatively geared property and a salary sacrifice arrangement can both cut your tax while leaving your HECS repayment untouched — or raising it. </p>\n<h2>Thresholds move every year</h2>\n<p> They are indexed to average weekly earnings. The minimum threshold went from  <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$67,000</span> in 2025–26 to  <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$69,528</span> in 2026–27. Switch the year selector above to see what applies to the year you are lodging, not the year you are in. </p>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n<section class=\"shell mt-20\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-help-hecs-repayment-calculator-heading\">\n<h2 id=\"faq-help-hecs-repayment-calculator-heading\" class=\"text-2xl\">Questions people actually ask</h2>\n<dl class=\"mt-6 border-t border-rule\">\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">What is the HECS repayment threshold for 2026-27?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">You start repaying once your repayment income passes <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$69,528</span>. Below that there is no compulsory repayment, whatever your loan balance.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">How is my HECS repayment calculated now?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Marginally, since 1 July 2025. You pay 15c on each dollar above the threshold, then 17c on income above the middle band. The old system charged a single rate on your entire income, so crossing a threshold by one dollar could cost hundreds — that cliff is gone.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Is repayment income the same as my salary?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">No, and this catches people out. Repayment income is your taxable income plus reportable fringe benefits, salary-sacrificed super, exempt foreign income and any net investment loss. Salary sacrificing into super lowers your tax but not your HECS repayment.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Should I pay my HECS off early?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Rarely worth it purely financially — HELP is indexed to inflation rather than charged interest, so it is among the cheapest debt available. It does affect borrowing capacity for a mortgage, which is the usual reason people clear it early.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">When is my loan indexed?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">On 1 June each year, applied to the balance outstanding at that point. Compulsory repayments made through your tax return are credited when the return is assessed, which can be after indexation.</dd>\n</p></div>\n</dl>\n</section>\n<section class=\"shell mt-20\">\n<h2 class=\"text-xl\">Read up first</h2>\n<ul class=\"mt-5 grid list-none gap-4 p-0 sm:grid-cols-2\">\n<li class=\"card p-5\">\n<h3 class=\"text-base\"><a href=\"/tax-tips/how-to-lodge-a-tax-return/\" class=\"text-ink no-underline hover:underline\">How to lodge your tax return</a></h3>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">The three ways to lodge an Australian tax return, what you need before you start, when to wait for pre-fill, and how the agent deadline extension works.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"cta-dark\">\n<div class=\"cta-grid\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"band-eyebrow\">Ready to lodge it?</p>\n<h2>A registered agent prepares it, checks it, and lodges it.</h2>\n<p>Most refunds land within two weeks of assessment. The fee is fixed and quoted before we start — nothing is charged until you approve the finished return.</p>\n<div class=\"cta-actions\"> <a href=\"https://brsadvisory.myassembly.com/login?step=signUp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"btn\">Start your return</a> <a href=\"/services/pricing/\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\">See pricing</a> </div>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec\">\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Individual returns from</span><b>$99</b></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Registered tax agent</span><b>26233684</b></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Fixed fee, quoted up front</span><i>included</i></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Fee taken from your refund</span><b>$44</b></div>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"shell mt-20\">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4\">\n<h2 class=\"text-xl\">Other calculators</h2>\n<p> <a href=\"/calculators/\" class=\"text-sm whitespace-nowrap\">All calculators →</a> </div>\n<ul class=\"mt-5 grid list-none gap-4 p-0 sm:grid-cols-3\">\n<li class=\"card p-5\"> <a href=\"/tax-calculator/\" class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink no-underline hover:underline\"> Income tax </a>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">Your tax, Medicare levy, study loan repayment and take-home pay for any income, in any of the last three financial years.</p>\n</li>\n<li class=\"card p-5\"> <a href=\"/tax-refund-calculator/\" class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink no-underline hover:underline\"> Tax refund </a>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">Estimate your refund by adding the deductions you actually have. Watch the number move as you claim.</p>\n</li>\n<li class=\"card p-5\"> <a href=\"/calculators/capital-gains-tax-calculator/\" class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink no-underline hover:underline\"> Capital gains </a>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">What you will pay on a share, property or crypto sale — with the 50% discount and any carried-forward losses applied in the right order.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<p><script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/brseeger-cloud/xyz-accounting-assets@main/islands/HelpCalculator.js\" defer></script></p>\n"
  },
